# SurfScaff3D: Bridging Geometric and Semantic Representations for LLM-based 3D Object Generation
@inproceedings{Loya2026SurfScaff3DBG,
  title={SurfScaff3D: Bridging Geometric and Semantic Representations for LLM-based 3D Object Generation},
  author={Anay Loya and Rishi Gupta and Arnav Samal and Anirban Chakraborty},
  year={2026},
  url={https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:295732455}
}
The Hierarchical Patch Scaffold (HPS) is introduced, a representation designed around semantically meaningful, interpretable part-level abstractions that are naturally understood by both humans and LLMs, enabling expressive, editable, and open-domain 3D generation without imposing restrictive geometric priors or expensive fine-tuning.
